PART IV — CLOUD STATE MACHINE

8. Required states

Each cloud hazard must support these six states:

State	Function
IDLE	The cloud stays stationary
HORIZONTAL	The cloud moves left and right
VERTICAL	The cloud moves up and down
DISAPPEARING	The cloud fades out
HIDDEN	The cloud is invisible and has no collision
REAPPEARING	The cloud fades in at a newly randomized valid position

These states must transition continuously throughout gameplay.

The cloud should never become permanently stuck in one state.

State-transition logic

When an ordinary state finishes, choose a new valid state randomly.

Possible ordinary choices are:

* IDLE.
* HORIZONTAL.
* VERTICAL.
* DISAPPEARING.

The disappearance lifecycle must follow:

DISAPPEARING → HIDDEN → REAPPEARING → next randomized ordinary state

A cloud cannot skip the hidden/reappearance lifecycle once disappearance begins.

The duration of ordinary states should be randomized.

Suggested tuning

Parameter	Starting range
Idle duration	1.5–4 seconds
Movement duration	2–5 seconds
Horizontal travel	60–140 world units
Vertical travel	35–90 world units
Disappearance fade	0.5–0.9 seconds
Hidden duration	1–2.5 seconds
Reappearance fade	0.5–0.9 seconds

These are initial guidelines.

Tune them against actual fighter movement speeds, jump heights, and platform sizes.

Keep all tuning centralized and configurable.

