PART VI — ZERO PLATFORM COLLISIONS

15. The three platforms must NEVER collide

This is an absolute gameplay requirement.

The following collisions must always be impossible:

* Main cloud with Cloud A.
* Main cloud with Cloud B.
* Cloud A with Cloud B.

This requirement applies at all times, including when clouds move, disappear, or reappear.

Safe movement regions

Assign each smaller cloud a bounded movement region.

The left cloud should generally occupy the upper-left part of the arena.

The right cloud should generally occupy the upper-right part.

Each region should leave sufficient horizontal and vertical clearance.

The movement regions must be designed so both hazards can move freely without ever physically intersecting.

Separation validation

Use actual platform bounds, including platform width, height, and safety margins.

Do not validate separation using only center points.

Account for:

* Horizontal movement.
* Vertical movement.
* Reappearance locations.
* Movement direction changes.
* Full collision widths.
* The main cloud’s upper surface.
* Relevant visual cloud volume.

Recommended guarantee

Prefer mathematically disjoint movement envelopes.

If both hazards’ complete possible movement envelopes cannot overlap, randomized movement remains safe by construction.

Also validate generated destinations.

A random movement destination must be rejected if it violates separation constraints.

If no valid movement destination exists, the cloud can temporarily enter IDLE.

No sudden corrections

Never allow a cloud to overlap another platform and then correct the mistake using visible teleportation.

Prevent invalid motion before it occurs.

The cloud must not clip into the main platform even for one simulation frame.

Disappeared clouds

A hidden cloud has no gameplay collision.

However, its future reappearance region must still be safe.

Do not rely on the fact that a cloud is hidden to permit an unsafe position that would become invalid when it reappears.

